      "prefLabel": "Adjudicator",
      "title": "Adjudicator",
      "notation": "adjudicator",
      "description": "Settles a criterion whose reviewer entries disagree, and records WHY. Inherits `reviewer` because an adjudicator is a reviewer with one added entitlement — the `adjudication` permission — and the separation is the point: a reviewer reports, an adjudicator settles, and a process where every reviewer could settle has no way to say who decided. The KNOWLEDGE spreads (several roles carry the `adjudication` skill, because each has to tell an adjudicable disagreement from a complaint); the ENTITLEMENT does not, and lives on the actor as a permission.",
